From 10050bafc57723432bd99b0750f03ab66df02677 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:43:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_wr_te_capacity_split and v2_vacancy_before_capacity

- v2_wr_te_capacity_split (2026-09-07, weeks 1-2): fit the WR and TE sub-rooms against separate budgets that split the off-budget
  delta by TE_MARGINAL_TARGET_WEIGHT (0.20). Shipped on, then pulled the same day once backtested: a wash on ALL at every weight with
  a significant WR / START-WR cost, and strictly worse than v2_receiver_cold_start_vacancy alone when stacked on it (lost ALL
  significance, START-TE significantly worse).
- v2_vacancy_before_capacity (2026-09-24): run vacancy before the pass-capacity pass to stop the Dowdle/Warren double count.
  INCONCLUSIVE with bias growth +0.359 (cap 0.3; START-ALL bias -0.337 -> -0.696) despite real WR / START-WR RMSE gains; the capacity
  pass's symmetric top-up corrects the model's under-projection when it runs last. The double count was fixed instead by the shipped
  v2_pass_capacity_injury_neutral_claim.
Removes wr_te_split / te_marginal_target_weight / TE_MARGINAL_TARGET_WEIGHT from the allocator, the two-order branch (capacity
then vacancy is now the only order), two sweep scripts and four split tests (the uniform-factor test stays).
Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
